boot: harb init -- machine qemu_own (hosted / x86_64 / qemu_pc) -- pid 1
boot: console /dev/ttyS0
boot: mount proc at /proc -- done
boot: mount sysfs at /sys -- done
boot: mount devtmpfs at /dev -- done
boot: mount ext4 at /data -- done
boot: grant filesystem (effectful)
boot: confine -- first has no sight of the other worlds and no way to start one, second has no sight of the other worlds and no way to start one; what a world did not declare, the kernel does not give it
boot: floor -- the machine is not a world's to change: none may mount or unmount, set the clock, load a module, rename the host, make or enter a namespace, trace another process, or reboot the box
boot: state -- first owns /data/alpha as alpha (2001:2001); second owns /data/beta as beta (2002:2002); each made, then read back as that identity's, mode 0700
boot: start first -- pid N -- /harb own /data/alpha --not /data/beta -- as alpha (2001:2001)
own: uid=2001 gid=2001
own: /data/alpha -- wrote note and read it back (6 bytes)
own: /data -- refused: AccessDenied
own: / -- refused: AccessDenied
own: /data/beta -- refused to list: AccessDenied
own: /data/beta -- refused to write: AccessDenied
own: this world wrote in its own directory and nowhere else
boot: first (pid N) exited 0
boot: start second -- pid N -- /harb own /data/beta --not /data/alpha -- as beta (2002:2002)
own: uid=2002 gid=2002
own: /data/beta -- wrote note and read it back (6 bytes)
own: /data -- refused: AccessDenied
own: / -- refused: AccessDenied
own: /data/alpha -- refused to list: AccessDenied
own: /data/alpha -- refused to write: AccessDenied
own: this world wrote in its own directory and nowhere else
boot: second (pid N) exited 0
boot: judge -- the boot matches its expectation (/etc/expected, 14 lines)
boot: every service has ended -- init has nothing left to keep alive
boot: init halts the machine -- reboot(RESTART)
reboot: Restarting system
disk: what the boot left on the disk, read back from the disk itself:
disk: / -- owned by 0:0, mode 0755
disk: /data/alpha -- owned by 2001:2001, mode 0700
disk: /data/alpha/note -- owned by 2001:2001, mode 0644
disk: /data/beta -- owned by 2002:2002, mode 0700
disk: /data/beta/note -- owned by 2002:2002, mode 0644
nodisk: the same image with no disk behind its mount:
nodisk: boot: harb init -- machine qemu_own (hosted / x86_64 / qemu_pc) -- pid 1
nodisk: boot: console /dev/ttyS0
nodisk: boot: mount proc at /proc -- done
nodisk: boot: mount sysfs at /sys -- done
nodisk: boot: mount devtmpfs at /dev -- done
nodisk: boot: mount ext4 at /data -- refused by the kernel: NOENT
nodisk: boot: grant filesystem (effectful)
nodisk: boot: confine -- first has no sight of the other worlds and no way to start one, second has no sight of the other worlds and no way to start one; what a world did not declare, the kernel does not give it
nodisk: boot: floor -- the machine is not a world's to change: none may mount or unmount, set the clock, load a module, rename the host, make or enter a namespace, trace another process, or reboot the box
nodisk: boot: state -- first was not given /data/alpha: the mount it lies on was refused by the kernel; a world that owns a directory it was not given does not start
nodisk: boot: state -- second was not given /data/beta: the mount it lies on was refused by the kernel; a world that owns a directory it was not given does not start
nodisk: boot: every service has ended -- init has nothing left to keep alive
nodisk: boot: init halts the machine -- reboot(RESTART)
nodisk: reboot: Restarting system
